{
  "note": "Spec 580 bars. Each bar judges one measured value of tools/measure_richness.sh: a min or max over the three bench poses (or one named pose), or a tint or fog field. A limit given per view applies to that view only. These are floors calibrated on the measured baseline and on the thin control; they never choose a picture. bare_near_frac allows 0.35 at far and vista: the meadow is drawn only to the view level's distance limit (a chunk's multimesh is culled by the distance of its centre), so ground 90 m and more away is bare by design; at near there is no limit and the floor is 0.30. far_ground_p90 is read at bench-ridge, the pose that looks at the horizon: at bench-river the camera looks down and at most 10 percent of its rays meet ground beyond 116 m whatever the ring or fog. Edge bars (Spec 580 S4) read the three edge poses of edge_poses.json: edge_gap_max is the share of the frame below the horizon line that still shows pure sky; floating_water_px_max counts water pixels with sky under them (the limit of 32 allows the 9 pixels of a hole in the lake mesh at the corner of the west edge pose, which the backdrop ring does not touch).",
